WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:05.806
A tree with five nodes, and you need its depth.

00:05.806 --> 00:14.700
Walking every root-to-leaf path visits the shared nodes again and again.

00:15.000 --> 00:23.532
Instead, ask each child how deep its side goes.

00:23.532 --> 00:31.700
An empty side answers 0, so a leaf answers 1.

00:32.000 --> 00:43.328
20 hears 1 from each side, takes the deeper, adds one: 2.

00:43.328 --> 00:47.700
Answers bubble upward.

00:48.000 --> 00:52.713
Each node answers once: O(n).

00:52.713 --> 00:55.313
The root says 3.

00:55.313 --> 00:59.700
That’s recursion on a tree.
